- `TestRankedMCP_CancelStopsIdleRead`: waits until the server enters a pipe read, cancels the context, observes no completion for 300 ms, then closes the fixture pipe to release the goroutine before failing. No leaked fixture reader.
- `TestRankedSSE_CursorOnlyAndEmptyReset`: uses the existing loopback fake server and streamOnce. Got empty instead of `new-cursor` for an ID-only frame; got `old` instead of empty after explicit reset. These are protocol cases from [WHATWG SSE processing](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html#event-stream-interpretation), not observed production server frames. Entire is a custom client, so confirm its advertised server contract before implementation.
